WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.425
So, four decisions.

2
00:00:01.425 --> 00:00:06.492
Name the classes and their owners: a small
register built from the C U I Registry,

3
00:00:06.492 --> 00:00:11.325
the Privacy Act and records schedules,
with an outcome an assessor can test.

4
00:00:11.325 --> 00:00:15.845
Publish a small taxonomy with safe
defaults: non-encrypting defaults,

5
00:00:15.845 --> 00:00:18.963
mandatory labeling, and
three container labels.

6
00:00:18.963 --> 00:00:22.367
Keep a tested way back in:
the super user feature off,

7
00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:27.150
recovery through an approved role,
and a decryption test every quarter.

8
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:31.948
And decide AI and evidence before rollout:
which labels Copilot may process,

9
00:00:31.948 --> 00:00:36.975
what oversharing gets fixed first, and a
monthly baseline the assessor can read.

10
00:00:36.975 --> 00:00:39.125
The next step needs no new tooling.

11
00:00:39.125 --> 00:00:42.102
Draft the class register
and the decision records,

12
00:00:42.102 --> 00:00:45.647
run a dated inventory with what
the tenant already licenses,

13
00:00:45.647 --> 00:00:49.475
and confirm each feature for your
own cloud before planning on it.

14
00:00:49.475 --> 00:00:51.638
Protection has to travel with the data.

15
00:00:51.638 --> 00:00:57.151
Information Protection and Microsoft Purview
has the detail, every claim footnoted.

16
00:00:57.151 --> 00:01:00.663
It's a draft, so check it again
after the editor's review.

17
00:01:00.663 --> 00:01:01.490
Thank you.
